Subject: CK: fix FMHA bwd path with sink (TransformerEngine integration)

fmha_bwd_kernel.hpp indexed sink_ptr as
`i_batch * nhead + i_nhead`, treating it as a [batch, nhead] buffer.
The sink buffer only holds one value per head (shape [nhead]), matching
how fwd kernels already read it, so batch_id must not factor into the
offset. Fixed to index by `i_nhead` alone, matching fwd.

diff --git a/3rdparty/composable_kernel/include/ck_tile/ops/fmha/kernel/fmha_bwd_kernel.hpp b/3rdparty/composable_kernel/include/ck_tile/ops/fmha/kernel/fmha_bwd_kernel.hpp
index 7aff21530..8ec6d9bad 100644
--- a/3rdparty/composable_kernel/include/ck_tile/ops/fmha/kernel/fmha_bwd_kernel.hpp
+++ b/3rdparty/composable_kernel/include/ck_tile/ops/fmha/kernel/fmha_bwd_kernel.hpp
@@ -1828,7 +1954,7 @@ struct FmhaBwdOGradDotOKernel
         const LSEDataType sink_value =
             kargs.sink_ptr != nullptr
                 ? log2e_v<LSEDataType> *
-                      kargs.sink_ptr[static_cast<long_index_t>(i_batch) * kargs.nhead + i_nhead]
+                      kargs.sink_ptr[static_cast<long_index_t>(i_nhead)]
                 : -numeric<LSEDataType>::infinity();
 
         // for simplicity, batch stride we just modify the pointer
